Lab 3 is a continuation of the memory card game. First step I copied my Lab 2 Xcode project and renamed it Lab 3. Then I modified the code implmenting
MVVM architecture by creating 3 groups View, ViewModel, and Model. I created 3 seperate swift files and placed them inside the corresponding
group folder. Inside the model MemoryGame I created the struct MemoryGame and inside it the variable required for the memory game. Also created struct Card
with assigned constants content and id, and variable isfaceup. These constants/variables will define the conent or image of the card, id, and whether or not
the card is facing up. I also initialized cards array using data from constant flowers and assigning an index number based on the location inside the 
flowers array.


Inside the ViewModel I created the class MemoryGameStore and added the protocal ObservableObject so the Views watch the ViewModel for any updates to the
state, in particular the flipcard function. Import combine was added because there were errors when using ObservableOject and this was required.  @Published
variable game was created to track MemoryGame() the model for any changes. If any changes are performed on the model, the ViewModel will notify the view
to refresh as required. Inside the ViewModel I also created the constant columns, this constant was added inside the ViewModel because import SwifUI was
imported for the ViewModel and its referenced in the View. Also the function flipcard was created that takes an argument that doesnt require an external 
parameter since the underscore was used. Inside the function a for loop is used to loop through every index inside the cards array that is inside the Model.
Inside the for loop an if statement compares the card tapped with each of the cards in the array in order to pinpoint the tapped cards exact location 
inside the cards array. For the tapped card when the correct location from the array is identified the function flipcard toggles, or flips, the boolean 
value of the variable isfaceup.

For the View, file ContentView.swift, I removed all the variables/constants that I declared inside the Model. I also removed the constant columns and 
changed how it was called out in the struct ContentView using the ViewModel, this was possible because @StateObject was added inside the ContentView struct.
No changes were done on the struct backcard. For the frontcard struct, I modified the If Else statement and removed the onTapGesture. I also added the transition
.rotation3DEffect with an easeinout animation. These transitions/animations are activated when a card is selected and using the onTapGesture which was moved to
the ContentView struct. ForEach was modified to use data from Model, making the ForEach less cluttered.

The differences between lab3 and lab2 was the implementation of the MVVM programming structure, which consists of a View, ViewModel, and Model. View creates
userinterface views, ViewModel is the translator of information between the View and Model, and the Model contains all data and logic. In addition a 
transition/animation was also implemented which rotates the tapped card either to show the front or back side.
